---
description: UMass Career Coach project rules (mirrors CLAUDE.md)
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow CLAUDE.md at the repo root. Key rules, repeated here:

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript strict + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui (Radix). Use shadcn components before writing custom ones.
- All shared types and zod schemas come from `lib/types.ts`. Never redefine them. Only B changes that file.
- Stay inside your owner's folders (see CLAUDE.md). Ask before editing another owner's files.
- Frontend fetches through one function per endpoint in `lib/api.ts`, which reads `mocks/*.json` until the real API exists.
- Never put secrets in client components or `NEXT_PUBLIC_` variables.
- Every Gemini output is validated with zod. Tailoring never invents skills, employers or numbers.
- Every page needs loading, empty and error states. Forms need labels and keyboard access.
- Small changes; `npm run build` must pass before committing.
